# Generated by artifacts/scripts/encode_paper.py from artifacts/kg/encoding/specs/poltavsky2025.yaml.
#
# Encoding scope: the MLFFs of the TEA Challenge 2023 (MACE, SO3krates,
# sGDML, SOAP/GAP and FCHL19*), trained by their developers in part 1 of
# the challenge (Ref. [61]) for four systems, used here in 12 MD
# trajectories per system and model. Observables (dihedral distributions,
# RDFs, adsorption heights, lattice dynamics) are compared between models
# and with DFT; no energy or force error is reported in this paper.

